00:00:46.065 --> 00:00:47.085
The formal charge, what?

00:00:47.085 --> 00:00:50.205
It uses a very simple formula
when it's all based on what

00:00:50.295 --> 00:00:51.675
our valence electrons are.

00:00:52.515 --> 00:00:54.885
And our Lewis structure
that we are drawing.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:01:00.645
So its formal charge is equal to the
number of valence electrons, minus

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:05.655
the number of lone pair electrons
that you have drawn around an atom.

00:01:06.105 --> 00:01:13.065
So for example, if I were to draw a,
let's say, um, let's say hydrogen for

00:01:13.065 --> 00:01:16.125
example, and I have just one little.here.

